rmat="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKANO, TOSHIAKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UMEZAWA, NORIO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA, OSAMU</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HOSODA TOSHIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKANO TOSHIAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UMEZAWA NORIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA OSAMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HOSODA, TOSHIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKANO, TOSHIAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UMEZAWA, NORIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA, OSAMU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An automatic painting device that prevents malfunction of a gripper (56) and poor painting due to nonfilling or insufficient filling of paint, and improves reliability. A cartridge gripping device (55) comprises a gripper (56) having a gripping pawl (66) for gripping a cartridge (25), a gripping state detecting switch (67) for detecting whether or not the gripper (56) grips the cartridge (25), and a filled state detecting switch (68) for detecting whether or not the cartridge (25) gripped by the gripper (56) is filled with paint. Thereby, when the cartridge (25) is gripped by the gripper (56), the gripping state detecting switch (67) is capable of confirming the gripping state of the cartridge (25). Further, the filled state detecting switch (68) is capable of confirming the filled state of the paint in the cartridge (25).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne un dispositif automatique de peinture, qui prévient la défaillance d'une griffe (56) et les manques de touche imputables à l'insuffisance totale ou partielle de peinture, et qui améliore la fiabilité. En l'occurrence, on utilise une tête de montage de cartouche (55) comprenant une griffe (56) à doigt d'encliquetage (66) saisissant une cartouche (25). La tête est également équipée d'un contact de détection de prise (67) permettant de constater ou non la saisie de la cartouche (25) par la griffe (56), et d'un contact de détection de niveau haut (68) permettant de constater ou non que la cartouche (25) saisie par la griffe () est remplie de peinture. Ainsi, lorsque la griffe (56) vient saisir la cartouche (25), le contact de détection de prise (67) est capable de confirmer la saisie de la cartouche (25), le contact de détection de niveau haut (68) étant alors à même de venir confirmer que la cartouche (25) est pleine de peinture.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>